From 2740dfa4c46d6e01c637c9c96cd874e82f13ace7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:59:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] sctp: Limit how much is queued below a socket

DRAFT prototype of TX small queues; see the comment in outqueue.c.  The
limit is net.sctp.limit_output_bytes, like tcp_limit_output_bytes, and is
off by default.  Needs review and Signed-off-by.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: LLM
